{"Admin group pagination computes totalPages with floor()+1 and Next can set offset==user_count, making an extra empty page reachable for exact multiples of limit (e.g. 100 users @ limit 50), causing the UI to show a bogus page count and render an empty members list on the last navigation step": 0.9270132780075073, "The remove_member controller spec uses PUT for the automatic-group rejection case, but the route and client use DELETE. This test can pass while the real DELETE integration is broken": 0.904187023639679, "The group member row template hides the remove link using {{#unless automatic}}, but row context is a member (Discourse.User), so automatic is undefined and the remove link is shown even for automatic groups. Clicking it triggers a 422 (server blocks automatic group membership changes) and the UI ignores the rejected promise": 0.9512404203414917}